    "title": "Watch: WVU volleyball reacts to near comeback vs. Kansas State - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Cody Nespor ,\n2 hours ago\nMORGANTOWN, W.Va. — West Virginia came just two points shy of pulling off an improbable comeback Wednesday night against Kansas State.\nWVU head coach Jen Greeny was proud of the way her team responded after falling down 2-0 to start the match. She said the Mountaineers simply made too many mistakes at the very end of the 3-2 loss.\nJunior outside hitter Nina Horning led West Virginia with a career-high 24 kills. She said the team being able to stay positive was why they were able to force a fifth set.\nClick on the videos above to watch both full press conferences.\nFollow Gold and Blue Nation on X , Facebook , Instagram and YouTube .\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to DC News Now | DC, Virginia, Maryland News, Weather, Traffic, Sports Live.",
